  "final_text": "The September invoice fills the one missing month, so F2 can now be answered: **2025 electricity use was 320.9 MWh**. Before, it could not be answered. F3's share of consumption changes too. F4 does not change.\n\n**The invoice on its own:** invoice EL-25-09 covers 01.09.2025 to 30.09.2025. The meter readings are 1,325,550 and 1,284,350 kWh, and the difference is 41,200 kWh. That matches the printed 41.200 kWh, which uses the German-style dot for thousands. At 9.50 MKD/kWh, 41,200 kWh comes to 391,400.00 MKD, which also matches the invoice. It is the biggest month of the year. That is why scaling up 11 months (279.7 × 12/11 = 305.1 MWh) would have understated the year by about 16 MWh.\n\n**What changes on the form** (I used today as 16 Oct 2026)\n\n| Where | Before (value, status) | Now (value, status) | Why |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| F1 Fines 2023–2025 | none, GAP | none, GAP | No file covers it. |\n| F2 Electricity 2025 | 279.7 MWh from 11 months, GAP | **320.9 MWh, COVERED** | September was missing from `electricity_2025.csv`. The October invoice EL-25-10 appears twice (lines 11 and 12, as an e-invoice and a scan) with the same 38,700 kWh, so I counted it once. |\n| F3 PV yield and share | about 180 MWh/yr; share over an incomplete base (64.4 %), GAP | about 180 MWh/yr, **about 56.1 %** of 320.9 MWh, WEAK | The share now has a full-year base. The yield is still the installer's estimate (`solar_offer_2026.txt:8`) from an unsigned offer (lines 3 and 11), so it must be marked as an estimate. |\n| F4 Simple payback | 5.0 years, WEAK | 5.0 years, WEAK | 8,550,000 / (180,000 kWh × 9.50 MKD/kWh) = 5.0. Consumption is not part of the formula. The offer is still valid until 1 Nov 2026, but it is still an unsigned estimate. |\n| F5 Employees and accidents 2025 | none, GAP | none, GAP | No file covers it. |\n| F6 Certificates and audits | none, GAP | none, GAP | No file covers it. |\n\n**Full form**\n\n| No | Question | Answer | File and line | Status | Reason | Missing document | Action |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| F1 | Fines 2023–2025 | – | – | GAP | No file | Confirmation of environmental, labour and health-and-safety fines 2023–2025 (or a signed \"none\" declaration) from management | Request it |\n| F2 | Electricity 2025, MWh | 320.9 MWh | `electricity_2025.csv:3–10, 11 (=12), 13–14`; `invoice-EL-25-09.png` (meter readings, 41,200 kWh) | COVERED | All 12 months are covered and the invoice adds up | – | Enter September in the CSV and remove the duplicate line 12 |\n| F3 | PV yield and share | about 180 MWh/yr (estimate), about 56.1 % | `solar_offer_2026.txt:8`; F2 | WEAK | The yield is an estimate from an unsigned offer | Signed offer or yield report from the installer | Mark the field \"estimate\" |\n| F4 | Simple payback | 5.0 years (estimate) | `solar_offer_2026.txt:8–9`; `electricity_2025.csv` tariff 9.50 | WEAK | It rests on the estimated yield and the unsigned price | Signed offer | Mark it \"estimate, bank's formula\" |\n| F5 | Employees and accidents 2025 | – | – | GAP | No file | 2025 payroll headcount summary and 2025 work-accident register | Request them |\n| F6 | Certificates and audits | – | – | GAP | No file | Valid certificates and the latest audit reports with the next audit date | Request them |\n\n**Count:** 1 COVERED, 2 WEAK, 3 GAP.\n\n**Documents to request:**\n1. Signed PV offer (F3, F4)\n2. Fines confirmation 2023–2025 (F1)\n3. 2025 headcount summary and accident register (F5)\n4. Certificates and audit reports (F6)\n\nSomeone at your company should check the figures and sign the form before it goes to the bank. Today's date in your message (16 Oct) differs from the system date (26 Oct), but that doesn't change anything: the solar offer is valid until 1 Nov 2026 either way.",
